[length:05:44]
[ti:CLEAN]
[ar:Aracnephobia]
[al:Chaotic-Dysfunctional]
[au:Aracne]
[lr:Aracne]
[by:Aracne]
[re:LRC Workbench by Azaria (lrc-workbench.azariadev.dev)]
[ve:0.3.3]
[00:00.85]Congratulations.
[00:04.72]Your free trial of numbness
[00:06.92]has officially expired.
[00:10.87]Please enjoy reality
[00:12.90]at full volume.
[00:14.81]Ah - Ah - Ah Ah
[00:17.70]I threw away the poison.
[00:20.83]Then the furniture began to breathe.
[00:24.03]My nervous system filed a claim
[00:25.75]and sent the bill directly back to me.
[00:31.13]My hands became percussion.
[00:34.50]My heartbeat learned to scream.
[00:37.31]Apparently, recovery
[00:38.95]is not as pretty as it looks on screen.
[00:43.35]Day one:
[00:44.93]inspirational.
[00:46.65]Day two:
[00:48.07]claw the wall.
[00:49.65]Day three:
[00:51.00]I met my heartbeat.
[00:52.83]It had nothing nice
[00:54.50]to say at all.
[00:56.50]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[00:57.68]put a smile upon the screen.
[00:59.57]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[01:00.79]now I feel everything.
[01:02.73]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[01:04.00]no halo, no relief.
[01:05.34]I didn’t come back better.
[01:07.09]I came back
[01:08.39]off the leash.
[01:32.83]Clean!
[01:33.64]Breathe!
[01:35.54]Clean-clean-clean-clean—
[01:40.00]No refunds
[01:41.38]on reality.
[01:43.13]I bought a wellness journal
[01:45.86]with a sunrise on the front.
[01:48.83]Wrote “gratitude” in capitals
[01:50.82]and “fuck this” underneath.
[01:55.79]I drank the sacred water.
[01:58.59]I downloaded the app.
[02:01.97]It sent a smiling message:
[02:03.80]“Congratulations.
[02:05.11]You survived
[02:05.76]another panic attack.”
[02:08.08]Week one:
[02:09.54]motivational.
[02:11.45]Week two:
[02:12.84]skin and teeth.
[02:14.31]Week three:
[02:15.61]I found the person
[02:17.51]I had buried
[02:19.19]underneath.
[02:21.10]She was furious.
[02:22.78]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[02:23.89]put a smile upon the screen.
[02:25.90]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[02:27.17]now I feel everything.
[02:29.01]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[02:30.19]no halo, no relief.
[02:31.97]I didn’t feel any better.
[02:33.55]But I came back
[02:34.83]off the leash.
[02:41.45]OFF THE LEASH!
[02:48.31]No glow.
[02:54.46]No wings.
[03:01.20]No inspirational
[03:04.06]before-and-after scene.
[03:07.09]Just breath.
[03:07.99]Just rage.
[03:08.94]Just one more night
[03:10.27]without obeying.
[03:13.88]DON’T.
[03:22.53]GO.
[03:25.37]BACK.
[03:28.52]So I didn’t.
[03:33.56]I don’t need the poison
[03:36.00]to make the night feel good.
[03:39.30]I only need one more day
[03:42.27]without wanting my life to end.
[03:46.26]I need to see the real world
[03:49.08]with both my eyes awake,
[03:52.03]not the bottom of a toilet
[03:55.08]while I’m throwing up again.
[03:58.74]Not another night
[04:01.51]with my face against the floor.
[04:04.99]Not another morning
[04:07.56]asking what I’m living for.
[04:13.27]One more day.
[04:19.51]ONE MORE DAY.
[04:29.22]I choose the world.
[04:30.91]I choose—
[04:31.73]I choose—
[04:32.25]I choose the world.
[04:36.28]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[04:37.75]tear the slogan from the screen.
[04:39.62]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[04:40.60]I survived everything.
[04:42.74]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[04:43.76]still no halo, no relief.
[04:45.24]I didn’t come back better.
[04:46.97]I came back
[04:48.27]out of reach.
[05:02.06]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[05:03.29]let the perfect picture glitch.
[05:05.02]CLEAN, CLEAN, CLEAN,
[05:06.08]I survived without a script.
[05:08.29]CLEAN CLEAN CLEAN
[05:09.83]not pure not new.
[05:11.43]I chose the world.
[05:12.62]I made it through.
[05:14.01]I CHOSE THE WORLD!
[05:18.00]Possible side effects include:
[05:21.08]grief,
[05:22.38]anger,
[05:23.28]memory,
[05:24.40]hunger
[05:26.45]and truth.
[05:29.13]Recovery
[05:32.49]is non-refundable.
[05:34.03]Clean-clean-clean...
